{"key":"enterprise/T1555.005","id":"T1555.005","name":"Password Managers","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1555","tactics":["credential-access"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may acquire user credentials from third-party password managers. Password managers are applications designed to store user credentials, normally in an encrypted database. Credentials are typically accessible after a user provides a master password that unlocks the database. After the database is unlocked, these credentials may be copied to memory. These databases can be stored as files on disk. Adversaries may acquire user…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/005","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--315f51f0-6b03-4c1e-bfb2-84740afb8e21","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:36.347Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0597","name":"Detect Unauthorized Access to Password Managers","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0597","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--a5600